---
source: crates/standalone/fixture/src/lib.rs
---
Link this folder to a site, without publishing it.

Usage: ink init [OPTIONS]

Examples
  # Make a site that takes uploads, and link this folder to it
  ink init --handle garden

  # Link this folder to a site that exists
  ink init --site 0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef

Options
      --handle <NAME>  Make a site with this handle, built from what `ink push`
                       sends, and link the folder to it
      --force          Replace a link the folder has to another site

Account
      --api <URL>          The API's address, `http://host[:port]`;
                           `account.api` in the config file [env: INK_API]
      --site <ID>          The site's id; `account.site` in the config file
                           [env: INK_SITE]
      --org <ID>           Act as this organization, by its id: the site is one
                           of its sites, and the key's role there is what is
                           checked. See `ink org list` [env: INK_ORG]
      --timeout <SECONDS>  Seconds one call may take [default: 30]
                           [env: INK_TIMEOUT]
      --retries <N>        How many more times a call that is safe to repeat is
                           tried when the network fails [default: 2]
                           [env: INK_RETRIES]
      --retry-wait <MS>    Milliseconds before the first retry; each wait is
                           twice the one before [default: 500]
                           [env: INK_RETRY_WAIT]

Notes
  Writes .uses/site, which holds the site's id and the API's address and no
  credential. A folder with no link refuses push, status, watch and export; the
  [account] table of the config file never stands in for it.

Exit codes
  0  Done
  2  Wrong usage: no site named, an id that is none, a deploy the site lacks
  3  Not signed in, or the token was refused
  4  The API could not be reached or failed; safe to retry
  5  The API refused the change as it stands: the deploy is already live, say

Environment
  INK_API       The address of the API, as --api
  INK_SITE      The site's id, as --site
  INK_KEY       The private key to sign requests with, for a CI job; never a
                flag, so it stays out of process lists. `ink login` keeps one in
                the config folder instead
  INK_KEY_FILE  A file that holds that key, in place of INK_KEY

See also  ink push, ink status
Docs      https://github.com/uses-ink/uses.ink/blob/main/docs/cli.md
Global    -C, --json, -q, -v, --color, --no-progress, --log, --log-file
          (see `ink --help`)
